Vendored numerical routines
===========================

R/arp-nuisance.R contains routines adapted from HonestDiD, authored by
Ashesh Rambachan and Jonathan Roth. Its original author notice is retained
in the source file. HonestDiD is distributed under the MIT license.
The installed HonestDiD 0.2.6 LICENSE metadata is preserved verbatim in
LICENSE-HonestDiD; the complete corresponding permission and warranty text
is in LICENSE-HonestDiD-MIT.

The remaining files (R/flci_core.R, R/inference_engine.R,
R/inference_adapter.R, and R/restriction_geometry.R) are numerical
extensions and adapters developed for the accompanying paper, Liu (2026),
"Cohort-Anchored HonestDiD". No separate conflicting license or third-party
copyright notice was found in those files. They are included under this
package's license; the preceding HonestDiD notice continues to apply to any
HonestDiD-derived portions.

Package adaptations include private resource loading, RNG-state preservation,
scalar target-basis and zero-nuisance LP cases, semidefinite-covariance
support, scale-relative ARP variance checks, and scale-relative M=0 FLCI
tie-breaking.

Referenced packages (including LP, normal-probability, and matrix libraries)
are dependencies and are not redistributed within these source files.

Methodological reference:
Rambachan, A. and Roth, J. (2023), "A More Credible Approach to Parallel
Trends," Review of Economic Studies, doi:10.1093/restud/rdad018.
